# docs/NATIVE-AGENTS.md §6.2 — "The decline/cancel distinction is not cosmetic and both must be
#   reachable": `[n] deny` lets the turn continue, `[esc] deny and stop` interrupts it
# docs/KEYMAP.md §Native agent thread — `y` · `a` · `n` · `e` · `Esc` on `AgentPermission`
#
# The other answer to the same gate, from the keyboard this time. `Enter` is deliberately not
# bound on a permission, so the only way to answer is the bare letter this scenario presses.
fixture: agents
await idle
key o
await screen == Workspace 20000

key ctrl-s A
await agents.threads[0].provider == codex 20000
assert focused == agents.composer
await idle 30000
type apply the README fix
key enter
await agents.threads[0].pending_gate == permission 30000
assert key_contexts[2] == AgentPermission && agents.threads[0].state == needs_you
shot approval

# `n` denies. The gate closes, the thread stops needing you, and the turn carries on with the
# change declined — Codex's `decline` does not interrupt the turn.
key n
await agents.threads[0].pending_gate absent 20000
assert agents.threads[0].state != needs_you && lists.tabs.selected.marks[0] != needs_you
await agents.threads[0].state == idle 30000
assert sticky_error absent
dump denied
quit
